{"type":"message","id":"3310e7a5","parentId":"6e30f76b","timestamp":"2026-04-06T07:06:10.561Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The remote is configured but the SSH host key verification failed. This is likely because SSH is trying to connect to github.com and the host key isn't verified. This typically happens in CI/automated environments.\n\nHowever, since this is a cron job running in the user's OpenClaw environment, and the push failed, I should note this in my response. The commit succeeded - the push is what's failing.\n\nLet me check if there's a way to handle this, but actually I should just report the status.","thinkingSignature":"5acf8dbce09a3b04f7a0ff0da203a5dbada7ac95e3ea21df61162e95bb501a59"},{"type":"text","text":"备份状态：\n\n✅ **已提交**：9 个文件已变更（591 行新增，19 行删除）\n❌ **推送失败**：SSH Host key 验证失败（`git push`）\n\n这是因为 cron 环境中的 SSH 配置缺少 GitHub 的 known_hosts 条目。需要手动推送或配置 SSH 密钥信任：\n\n```bash\nssh-keyscan github.com >> ~/.ssh/known_hosts 2>/dev/null\n```\n\n之后重新触发推送即可。"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":520,"output":199,"cacheRead":11566,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":12285,"cost":{"input":0.000156,"output":0.00023879999999999998,"cacheRead":0.00069396,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0010887599999999998}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1775459161887,"responseId":"06228e5abd06ebb47a96332fac5551a8"}}
